      "statement": "All KG access goes over Bolt through the shared KgClient; reads run in read transactions (which Memgraph rejects writes in — the primary write guard for the user query path) and writes in write transactions with driver-side transient-error retry, except that 'memory limit exceeded' is deliberately converted to a non-retried MemoryLimitError in both libraries.",
